2. Row count drifts when someone edits the grid. Cure: test pins 11 rows.
3. A row grows past 27 cols and collides with the text column. Cure: test pins width.

## hoare — contract breaks
4. Width read from process.stdout inside the lib makes the test need a TTY.
   Cure: width is an argument.
5. Version hardcoded in the grid drifts from package.json. Cure: interpolated.

## norman — the adopter misreads it
6. Narrow terminal wraps the mark; adopter reads corruption. Cure: drop below 53.
7. Mark lands in --json stdout and breaks a parser. Cure: same !json guard as
   VALUE_TEST_BLOCK; parity test asserts no block glyph in json stdout.
